sequenceDiagram
  title: Shutdown — Ordered Teardown (app::destroy)

  participant MAIN as main / CLI
  participant WEBVIEW as webview_run
  participant DISPATCH as dispatch.shutdown
  participant APP as app.destroy — App
  participant LIFECYCLE as lifecycle.unregisterEvents
  participant WINDOW as window.destroyWindow
  participant CMD as commands.destroy
  participant LUA as lua.destroy — Runtime
  participant BRIDGE as bridge.destroy
  participant CTX as context.destroy

  WEBVIEW -->> MAIN : webview_run returns — native window closed
  MAIN ->> DISPATCH : dispatch::shutdown(app)
  DISPATCH ->> DISPATCH : drain remaining messages — final flush
  DISPATCH ->> DISPATCH : remove CFRunLoopSource

  MAIN ->> APP : app::destroy(app)

  APP ->> LIFECYCLE : lifecycle::unregisterEvents — stop resize/focus observers
  APP ->> WINDOW : destroyWindow — free views (View* per registered name)
  APP ->> CMD : commands::destroy — BEFORE Lua (handlers hold sol functions)
  APP ->> LUA : lua::destroy → delete sol::state
  APP ->> BRIDGE : bridge::destroy → delete transport + store
  APP ->> CTX : context::destroy

  APP ->> APP : webview_destroy last — platform teardown after transport/window gone
  APP -->> MAIN : delete app
  MAIN -->> MAIN : return 0

  @start_note right of LUA
    Order matters: commands hold sol::function
    references into the Lua state — destroying Lua
    first would leave dangling function bindings.
  @end_note